/* exists a. P(a + a + a) with P(x) the singleton x = 1: invalid over the integers, since 3a = 1 has
   no solution.  The optimizer's quantifier erasure once read a + a + a as onto in a (a variable
   occurring an odd number of times under additions was taken to be adjustable) and replaced the
   query by exists y. P(y), which is valid. */
exists (a: int). P (a + a + a)
s.t.
P (x: int): bool =mu x = 1;
